{% doc %}
  blocks/section-header.liquid

  The heading cluster that opens a section: an eyebrow, a headline, a line of
  supporting copy, and a call to action.

  ## Why it is a group underneath

  Everything this needs — direction, alignment, distribution, gaps, width,
  background, border, padding, the mobile stack — is what `blocks/group.liquid`
  already does, and it does it through `snippets/group.liquid`. A second
  implementation of that would be a second set of layout bugs, and the two would
  drift the first time somebody adjusts a gap in one of them.

  So this block renders the same snippet, with the same setting ids and the same
  translation keys. What it adds is a *name* — `.block-section-header` plus a
  modifier for the direction — which is the hook the two presets and the
  stylesheet hang off. A merchant who has learned the Group block already knows
  every control in here.

  ## Two presets, one file

  **Vertical** stacks the whole cluster and centres it. **Horizontal** is a row
  with the copy on the left and the button on the right, held apart by
  `space-between`, so the button sits opposite the text rather than under it.

  The horizontal preset nests a group for the left-hand side, and that nesting is
  what makes the two sides real: the copy is a column that owns its own gap and
  can take further blocks, and the button is its sibling. Splitting the two sides
  in CSS instead would mean guessing which child is the button, and would break
  silently the moment a merchant adds a second one.

  ## Extending it

  Both presets accept `@theme` and `@app` blocks, so anything the theme offers
  can join the cluster. In the horizontal preset a new block dropped into the
  left-hand group joins the copy; dropped at the top level it becomes a third
  column of the row.

  ## The heading gradient

  Nothing here paints it. The heading is an ordinary Text block on the `h2`
  preset with its own **Colour › Gradient** filled in by the preset, so the
  gradient arrives with the block and the merchant changes it in the same place
  they would change any other text colour.
  `snippets/block-typography.liquid` turns that into `--block-text-gradient` and
  `base.css` owns the clip — the same path every other gradient heading in the
  theme takes.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  # The direction control is the group's own, so the modifier is derived from it
  # rather than stored a second time. A merchant who switches a vertical section
  # header to Horizontal gets the horizontal behaviour, with no second setting
  # left free to disagree with the first.
  assign layout = 'vertical'
  if block.settings.direction == 'row'
    assign layout = 'horizontal'
  endif

  assign extra_classes = 'block-section-header block-section-header--' | append: layout
-%}

{%- capture children -%}
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
{%- endcapture -%}

{% render 'group',
   children: children,
   settings: block.settings,
   extra_classes: extra_classes,
   shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes %}

